 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No clothing, nakedness, garden or figure drawn; the Shaytan and his kind never drawn and no motif during 27. An hourglass for life and death, light for «ولباس التقوى». First-person «جعلنا» (26, 27) not used. STAGING v4: c1 (25: on the earth you live, die and are brought out): people in fields by day (Muyassar: on the earth you spend your worldly life); the fields grow on 25:3 (you live), an hourglass on 25:4 for the term; nobody leaves on the word of death and the resurrection is not pictured. c2 (26: clothing that covers, and adornment): a market street; a group in plain covering clothes (camera on them at 26:6) and a man in fine robes for the adornment (26:9, Muyassar: clothing for adornment and beauty) with a jewel plate; on the clothing of piety (26:10) a light plate and a soft sparkle on the group (As-Sa'di: the beauty of the heart and soul); on 26:19 (that they may remember) they look up. Only men are drawn; nothing about nakedness is shown. c3 (27: the Shaytan who removed the parents from the Garden and sees you unseen) stays ambient with no motif: the Garden, the uncovering, the Shaytan and his kind are not drawn."
 },
